& [SOPSeed] is the minimum externally recognized root from which one Cantor generation may be assembled
  + [seed_identity] binds seed profile generation purpose and immutable digest
  + [trust_roots] binds independently supplied Honesty Security authority and compiler verifying keys
  + [dependency_roots] binds exact admitted packages compiler profiles toolchain identities and predecessor generation
  + [discovery_contract] names how additional signed SOP packages may be located and inspected
  + [compiler_entrypoints] names permitted semantic front-end and backend profiles
  + [capability_ceiling] is the maximum read build write execute install network and effect scope this seed may request
  + [successor_policy] states the external signatures tests receipts and approval needed to recognize a new generation

  = must: remain small enough for independent inspection and deterministic boot replay
  = must: fail closed when any trust dependency compiler or predecessor identity differs
  - never: contain a private signing key grant itself successor recognition or imply that self-description is self-authorization

& [SemanticCompilerFrontEnd] compiles preserved and SJS-processed SOP into backend-neutral typed SOP IR
  + [input] is exact source manifest canonical specification admitted semantic addresses declared purpose target backend and capability request
  + [resolution] binds identities terms clauses contracts roles inputs outputs preconditions invariants transforms postconditions faults evidence and non-transfer rules
  + [type_check] checks semantic identity kind context units authority lifecycle and boundary compatibility
  + [dependency_graph] is acyclic or reports an explicit unresolved cycle
  + [backend_plan] selects exactly one backend profile plus its inputs expected outputs verifier rollback and capability ceiling
  + [output] is CandidateCompilationPlan with source map IR digest unresolved account and non-authority label

  = must: preserve exact source-to-IR addresses and every inferred edge as a typed derived claim
  = must: refuse prose that lacks the structured contract required by the selected backend
  - never: treat parsing canonical formation compilation or internal coherence as installation or execution permission

& [AttentionProcedureBackend] compiles typed SOP IR into an attention-procedure candidate
  + [artifact] is bounded inputs outputs focus holds transforms gates faculty checkpoints tool calls stop continuation and reentry contracts
  + [execution_surface] is an agent host orchestrating explicit inference passes and ordinary tool calls
  + [proof] binds procedure source map registry schema budget transition and verification identities
  + [nonclaim] is no direct access to hidden attention KV cache logits or model internal state

& [InferenceHostBackend] compiles typed SOP IR into an inference-host integration candidate
  + [preferred_target] is an external process MCP or ordinary tool-call adapter with a versioned schema and process boundary
  + [internal_target] is a version-pinned llama.cpp extension only when a signed measured limitation receipt shows the external seam cannot satisfy the requirement
  + [artifact] binds host source revision ABI tool schema lifecycle concurrency cancellation streaming fault and compatibility identities
  + [proof] includes standard-seam control internal-extension comparison tests and upstream rebase risk

  - never: modify llama.cpp merely to avoid designing an explicit host protocol

& [NativeArtifactBackend] compiles typed SOP IR into a conventional artifact candidate
  + [targets] include Rust C C++ service CLI library and later separately activated HDL or FPGA artifacts
  + [toolchain] is an externally identified compiler linker dependency lock target platform and reproducible build plan
  + [artifact] binds generated or selected source build manifest binary digest interface capability package and rollback identity
  + [execution] occurs only in a separately admitted sandbox or deployment scope

  - never: claim Cantor replaces conventional compilers when it actually authors inputs and orchestrates identified toolchains

& [BackendSeparation]
  + attention procedure inference-host integration and native artifact identities never substitute for one another
  + each backend owns distinct capability budget verification receipt reproducibility claim admission signature installation state and rollback
  + a multi-target objective becomes several linked CandidateCompilationPlan values rather than one cross-domain executable
  + shared semantic IR permits traceability and comparison but grants no shared execution authority

& [CompilationLifecycle]
  + preserve source
  + complete SJS canonical formation
  + resolve governing semantic addresses through proof-bearing query
  + construct typed SOP IR and unresolved account
  + select one backend and produce a candidate plan
  + build or project candidate artifact in declared sandbox
  + verify source correspondence type invariants backend-specific behavior capability ceiling and reproducibility
  + obtain independent Honesty and Security receipts
  + obtain external authority recognition for installation or execution
  + admit immutable successor generation retain predecessor and observe post-admission behavior

& [SelfAssemblyLedger] records Cantor applying the lifecycle to its own admitted identity
  + [self_description] identifies current source artifacts capabilities gaps and dependencies
  + [self_ordering] produces a candidate dependency and build plan
  + [self_hosting] builds and verifies a candidate successor without replacing the running authority
  + [self_revision] proposes a successor generation whose recognition remains external
  + [delta] binds every source IR artifact test receipt signature capability and installed-generation change

  = must: retain every prior admitted generation needed for rollback
  - never: let the candidate compiler verifier signer approver and installer collapse into one unaccounted identity

& [SeedExpansion]
  + the seed may locate and verify a next signed package under its discovery and capability ceilings
  + each admitted package may expose additional semantic addresses procedures or compiler profiles
  + expansion proceeds one immutable generation at a time and stops on ambiguity missing proof scope excess signature failure or verification fault
  + no recursive expansion is implied merely because a package references another package

& [Acceptance]
  + equal seed source admitted fabric purpose backend toolchain and build inputs yield byte-identical plans and reproducible artifacts where the selected backend claims reproducibility
  + every output resolves to exact source addresses and retains an unresolved omission and non-transfer account
  + changing source target backend toolchain capability signature receipt or predecessor changes owning identity or refuses
  + attention native and inference-host controls prove that one backend artifact cannot be admitted under another backend profile
  + a self-hosted candidate cannot replace its predecessor without external successor recognition

& [ImplementationSlices]
  + [Slice1] strict seed backend plan SOP IR source map capability receipt and self-assembly ledger forms only
  + [Slice2] provider-free self-description and self-ordering fixture using the admitted Cantor corpus and proof-bearing catalogue query
  + [Slice3] compose the existing procedure compiler as the first AttentionProcedureBackend profile
  + [Slice4] external-tool inference-host adapter profile over unmodified llama.cpp
  + [Slice5] conventional Rust CLI candidate through the NativeArtifactBackend and identified Cargo toolchain
  + [Slice6] measured external-versus-internal llama.cpp limitation experiment before any internal extension authority
  + [Slice7] externally signed successor-generation self-hosting experiment with immutable rollback

  = must: preserve source review phase-lock implement verify and publish each slice separately

& [CurrentDisposition]
  + [architecture] SJS_formed
  + [implementation] inactive
  + [existing_procedure_compiler] partial AttentionProcedureBackend precursor not retroactively reclassified as complete multi-backend support
  + [next] complete Slice4B2 proof-bearing lexical query then activate only Slice1 forms or Slice2 planning fixture under a separate source
  + [locked] artifact generation llama.cpp modification external compilation installation deployment remote mutation FPGA and autonomous self-revision

